---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GitHubLink from '../../../components/GitHubLink.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CSS styles chain · HCI Nerdz"
  description="Inspect the element you clicked as properties with a chain: important rules that lost, the one in effect, and inherited values that no longer apply."
  active="demos"
>
  <main class="shell page desk-page css-styles-chain-page">
    <nav class="identity-strip" aria-label="Demo identity">
      <a href="/">HCI Nerdz</a>
      <span class="identity-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/demos/">Demos</a>
      <span class="identity-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">CSS styles chain</span>
    </nav>
    <p class="vcs-row">
      <GitHubLink href="https://github.com/HCI-Nerdz/HCI-Nerdz.github.io" showStars={false} />
    </p>

    <header class="desk-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Demo · CSS styles chain</p>
      <h1>CSS styles chain</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Pick an element and edit the properties that actually apply to it. Each property is a chain:
        important declarations that lost, the one in effect, then ordinary and inherited declarations
        that no longer apply. A selector that missed this element never appears.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="demo-controls" aria-label="Demo controls">
      <h2>Demo controls</h2>
      <p>
        Theme is the page under inspection, not a switch in the inspector. Dark adds one real rule
        from the stylesheet. Light leaves it out, because it does not match.
      </p>
      <div class="theme-picks" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Page theme">
        <label><input type="radio" name="page-theme" value="light" checked /> Light page</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="page-theme" value="dark" /> Dark page</label>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="facsimile-bezel">
      <div class="win-caption">
        <span class="win-title">CSS styles chain</span>
        <span class="win-controls" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i class="win-close"></i></span>
      </div>
      <div class="inspector">
        <p class="legend" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="key key-lost-imp">! lost</span>
          <span class="key key-active">in effect</span>
          <span class="key key-natural">ordinary or inherited, inactive</span>
        </p>
        <div id="inspector-body"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="lesson">
      <h2>What the long selector is</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>One test, read from the outside in.</strong>
          <code>.doc .openblock.cards .exampleblock.tile &gt; .content</code>
          matches only if every piece matches. The div you clicked has class
          <code>content</code>. <code>tile</code> and <code>exampleblock</code> are on its parent.
          <code>openblock</code> and <code>cards</code> are on a further ancestor.
          <code>doc</code> is further still. It does not mean the div carries all of those classes,
          and one class on the div is not enough.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Grey names after a comma are a failed alternative.</strong>
          <code>.doc .exampleblock &gt; .content, .doc details.result &gt; .content</code>
          is two selectors. The comma means “or”. DevTools greys
          <code>.doc details.result &gt; .content</code> because this div is not inside
          <code>details.result</code>. Those grey tokens are not classes on your element.
          This desk omits the half that missed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>(0, 6, 0) is six classes.</strong>
          The hover triple is (ids, classes, element names).
          <code>.content</code> is a class, so it counts in the middle number.
          The <code>&gt;</code> adds nothing. DevTools prints the triple and does not say that.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The nest is two trees drawn as one list.</strong>
          Ancestry is a tree. Each property is a short stack of declarations that matched.
          DevTools flattens both into selector cards, including rules that matched an ancestor
          and alternatives that matched nothing. The chain keeps the stack, and the element
          tree keeps the ancestry.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The chain is a number, not the selector.</strong>
          <code>class 5</code> is one stylesheet rule. The line stays short enough to scan.
          Opening the number inserts that one rule under the property. The triangle at the
          end of the line is the only control that opens every class. The cards are indented by how far the selector
          reaches into the element tree. A loss says which number beat it, in that card,
          not under the rest of the list.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The property you asked about stays the subject.</strong>
          In DevTools, the jump is named “View computed value”, sits last in the right-click
          menu, and has no icon. It opens a tab called Computed, leaves the box-model diagram
          up, and filters by that word. Asking about <code>background</code> then lists
          <code>background-color</code>, <code>background-image</code>, and every other name
          that contains the word, at the same weight. Here, a losing crumb says what beat it.
          Names that only share the word sit under that property, in grey, after the chain.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .css-styles-chain-page {
    max-width: 72rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .identity-strip {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.35rem 0.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .identity-strip a {
    color: var(--paper-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .identity-strip a:hover {
    color: var(--focus);
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .identity-sep {
    opacity: 0.45;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .vcs-row {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .desk-intro .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--honesty);
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .lede-shot {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .lede-shot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 12px;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .lede-shot figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--paper-muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .demo-controls {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper) 35%, transparent);
    border-radius: 12px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .demo-controls h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .demo-controls p {
    margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .theme-picks {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .theme-picks label {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    align-items: center;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .facsimile-bezel {
    border: 1px solid #c5c1b6;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #f4f2ec;
    color: #1c1b19;
    box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .win-caption {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    background: #f7f7f7;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e1e1e1;
    font-family: "Segoe UI", var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .win-controls {
    display: flex;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .win-controls i {
    width: 2.4rem;
    height: 1.55rem;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    position: relative;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .win-controls i::before,
  .css-styles-chain-page .win-controls i::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    background: #1c1b19;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .win-controls i:nth-child(1)::before {
    left: 0.7rem;
    right: 0.7rem;
    top: 0.85rem;
    height: 1px;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .win-controls i:nth-child(2)::before {
    left: 0.75rem;
    top: 0.45rem;
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.55rem;
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid #1c1b19;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .win-controls i:nth-child(3)::before,
  .css-styles-chain-page .win-controls i:nth-child(3)::after {
    left: 0.7rem;
    top: 0.7rem;
    width: 0.85rem;
    height: 1px;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .win-controls i:nth-child(3)::before {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .win-controls i:nth-child(3)::after {
    transform: rotate(-45deg);
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .inspector {
    padding: 0.75rem;
    font-family: "Segoe UI", var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .key {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .key::before {
    content: "";
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .key-lost-imp::before {
    background: #9b2c2c;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .key-active::before {
    background: #1f7a3a;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .key-natural::before {
    background: #8a8478;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .inspector-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 16rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .css-styles-chain-page .inspector-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .tree-pane,
  .css-styles-chain-page .prop-pane,
  .css-styles-chain-page .crumb-detail {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #ddd8ce;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.7rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .pane-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6d675f;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .elem-tree,
  .css-styles-chain-page .elem-tree ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .elem-tree ul {
    margin-left: 0.85rem;
    border-left: 1px solid #e4dfd4;
    padding-left: 0.45rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .elem-btn {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    background: transparent;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.35rem;
    font: inherit;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .elem-btn code {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .is-selected > .elem-btn {
    background: #e7f5ec;
    border-color: #1f7a3a;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .is-hit > .elem-btn {
    background: #fff4e5;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .is-selected.is-hit > .elem-btn {
    background: #e7f5ec;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .status-line {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    color: #5c574f;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .prop-row {
    padding: 0.55rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #eeeae2;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .prop-row:first-of-type {
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .prop-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .prop-name {
    font-family: Consolas, ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-weight: 700;
    min-width: 7.5rem;
    text-align: left;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .prop-row.is-subject {
    background: #fffdf8;
    margin: 0 -0.35rem;
    padding-left: 0.35rem;
    padding-right: 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .related {
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.55rem;
    background: #f3f1ec;
    color: #8a8478;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .related p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .related ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem 0.7rem;
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .related li {
    font-family: Consolas, ui-monospace, monospace;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .beaten-by {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .beaten-by button {
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #1f7a3a;
    background: #e5f6ea;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.12rem 0.55rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .prop-head input[type='text'] {
    flex: 1 1 12rem;
    font-family: Consolas, ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.4rem;
    border: 1px solid #d5d0c6;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #fff;
    color: #1c1b19;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .imp-toggle {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: #6d675f;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .chain {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .chain li {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .chain-sep {
    color: #b0aaa0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .crumb {
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.12rem 0.5rem;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .expand-all {
    width: 1.4rem;
    height: 1.4rem;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .expand-all::before {
    content: "";
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    border-style: solid;
    border-width: 0.36rem 0.5rem 0.36rem 0;
    border-color: transparent #3f3b36 transparent transparent;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .expand-all[aria-expanded='true']::before {
    border-width: 0.5rem 0.36rem 0 0.36rem;
    border-color: #3f3b36 transparent transparent transparent;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .class-stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .class-card {
    border: 1px solid #e4dfd4;
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.55rem;
    background: #fff;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .class-card.is-active {
    border-color: #1f7a3a;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .class-card.is-important-lost {
    border-color: #9b2c2c;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .class-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .crumb-important-lost {
    background: #f8e8e8;
    color: #9b2c2c;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .crumb-active {
    background: #e5f6ea;
    color: #1f7a3a;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .crumb-natural-lost {
    background: #f3f1ec;
    color: #8a8478;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .crumb[aria-pressed='true'] {
    outline: 2px solid #e8a54b;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .crumb-detail {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .crumb-detail h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .anatomy {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0.4rem 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .anatomy li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 14rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.2rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #eeeae2;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .css-styles-chain-page .anatomy li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .anatomy code {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .css-styles-chain-page .reason {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
  }
</style>

<script>
  type NodeId = 'body' | 'article' | 'cards' | 'tile' | 'content';
  type Kind = 'important-lost' | 'active' | 'natural-lost';

  interface Anatomy {
    piece: string;
    need: string;
  }

  interface Decl {
    id: string;
    property: string;
    value: string;
    important: boolean;
    specificity: [number, number, number];
    order: number;
    source: string;
    selector: string;
    label: string;
    hits: NodeId[];
    inline?: boolean;
    match: (id: NodeId, theme: string) => boolean;
    anatomy: Anatomy[];
  }

  const PARENT: Record<NodeId, NodeId | null> = {
    body: null,
    article: 'body',
    cards: 'article',
    tile: 'cards',
    content: 'tile',
  };

  const NODE_LABEL: Record<NodeId, string> = {
    body: 'body',
    article: 'article.doc.valentus-article',
    cards: 'div.openblock.cards',
    tile: 'div.exampleblock.tile',
    content: 'div.content',
  };

  const OWN_CLASSES: Record<NodeId, string> = {
    body: '(no classes)',
    article: 'doc  valentus-article',
    cards: 'openblock  cards',
    tile: 'exampleblock  tile',
    content: 'content',
  };

  const tileAnatomy: Anatomy[] = [
    { piece: '.doc', need: 'An ancestor has class doc.' },
    { piece: '.openblock.cards', need: 'An ancestor has both openblock and cards.' },
    { piece: '.exampleblock.tile', need: 'The parent has both exampleblock and tile.' },
    { piece: '> .content', need: 'The element you picked has class content.' },
  ];

  const contentHits: NodeId[] = ['article', 'cards', 'tile', 'content'];

  function tileDecl(
    id: string,
    property: string,
    value: string,
    order: number,
    source: string,
    label: string,
  ): Decl {
    return {
      id,
      property,
      value,
      important: false,
      specificity: [0, 6, 0],
      order,
      source,
      selector: '.doc .openblock.cards .exampleblock.tile > .content',
      label,
      hits: contentHits,
      match: (nodeId) => nodeId === 'content',
      anatomy: tileAnatomy,
    };
  }

  const DECLS: Decl[] = [
    {
      id: 'body-color',
      property: 'color',
      value: 'CanvasText',
      important: false,
      specificity: [0, 0, 1],
      order: 1,
      source: 'the page',
      selector: 'body',
      label: 'body',
      hits: ['body'],
      match: (id) => id === 'body',
      anatomy: [{ piece: 'body', need: 'This element is the body.' }],
    },
    {
      id: 'body-font',
      property: 'font-family',
      value: 'serif',
      important: false,
      specificity: [0, 0, 1],
      order: 1,
      source: 'the page',
      selector: 'body',
      label: 'body',
      hits: ['body'],
      match: (id) => id === 'body',
      anatomy: [{ piece: 'body', need: 'This element is the body.' }],
    },
    {
      id: 'article-color',
      property: 'color',
      value: 'var(--valentus-ink)',
      important: false,
      specificity: [0, 1, 0],
      order: 10,
      source: 'site.visual.css',
      selector: '.valentus-article',
      label: 'article',
      hits: ['article'],
      match: (id) => id === 'article',
      anatomy: [
        { piece: '.valentus-article', need: 'This element has class valentus-article.' },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'article-font',
      property: 'font-family',
      value: 'Source Sans 3',
      important: false,
      specificity: [0, 1, 0],
      order: 10,
      source: 'site.visual.css',
      selector: '.valentus-article',
      label: 'article',
      hits: ['article'],
      match: (id) => id === 'article',
      anatomy: [
        { piece: '.valentus-article', need: 'This element has class valentus-article.' },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'tile-display',
      property: 'display',
      value: 'flex',
      important: false,
      specificity: [0, 5, 0],
      order: 20,
      source: 'valentus-chrome.css',
      selector: '.doc .openblock.cards .exampleblock.tile',
      label: 'tile box',
      hits: ['article', 'cards', 'tile'],
      match: (id) => id === 'tile',
      anatomy: [
        { piece: '.doc', need: 'An ancestor has class doc.' },
        { piece: '.openblock.cards', need: 'An ancestor has both openblock and cards.' },
        { piece: '.exampleblock.tile', need: 'This element has both exampleblock and tile.' },
      ],
    },
    tileDecl('chrome-bg', 'background', 'var(--doc-tile-background)', 20, 'valentus-chrome.css', 'tile rule, earlier sheet'),
    tileDecl('chrome-border', 'border', '1px solid var(--doc-tile-border-color)', 20, 'valentus-chrome.css', 'tile rule, earlier sheet'),
    tileDecl('chrome-flex', 'flex', '1 1 auto', 20, 'valentus-chrome.css', 'tile rule, earlier sheet'),
    tileDecl('chrome-pad', 'padding', '1.25rem 1.25rem 1rem', 20, 'valentus-chrome.css', 'tile rule, earlier sheet'),
    tileDecl('chrome-display', 'display', 'flex', 20, 'valentus-chrome.css', 'tile rule, earlier sheet'),
    tileDecl('brand-bg', 'background', 'var(--doc-tile-background, Canvas)', 30, 'devcentr-brand.css', 'tile rule, later sheet'),
    tileDecl('brand-border', 'border', '1px solid var(--doc-tile-border-color, GrayText)', 30, 'devcentr-brand.css', 'tile rule, later sheet'),
    tileDecl('brand-flex', 'flex', '1 1 auto', 30, 'devcentr-brand.css', 'tile rule, later sheet'),
    tileDecl('brand-pad', 'padding', '1.25rem 1.25rem 1rem', 30, 'devcentr-brand.css', 'tile rule, later sheet'),
    tileDecl('brand-display', 'display', 'flex', 30, 'devcentr-brand.css', 'tile rule, later sheet'),
    {
      id: 'example-bg',
      property: 'background',
      value: 'var(--valentus-elevated)',
      important: true,
      specificity: [0, 3, 0],
      order: 25,
      source: 'site.visual.css',
      selector: '.doc .exampleblock > .content',
      label: 'example block !important',
      hits: ['article', 'tile', 'content'],
      match: (id) => id === 'content',
      anatomy: [
        { piece: '.doc', need: 'An ancestor has class doc.' },
        { piece: '.exampleblock', need: 'The parent has class exampleblock. cards is not required.' },
        { piece: '> .content', need: 'The element you picked has class content.' },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'example-border',
      property: 'border',
      value: '1px solid var(--valentus-border)',
      important: true,
      specificity: [0, 3, 0],
      order: 25,
      source: 'site.visual.css',
      selector: '.doc .exampleblock > .content',
      label: 'example block !important',
      hits: ['article', 'tile', 'content'],
      match: (id) => id === 'content',
      anatomy: [
        { piece: '.doc', need: 'An ancestor has class doc.' },
        { piece: '.exampleblock', need: 'The parent has class exampleblock. The tile and cards classes are irrelevant to this test.' },
        { piece: '> .content', need: 'The element you picked has class content.' },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'dark-bg',
      property: 'background',
      value: 'var(--doc-tile-background)',
      important: true,
      specificity: [0, 7, 1],
      order: 60,
      source: 'valentus-chrome.css',
      selector: 'html.dark-theme .doc .openblock.cards .exampleblock.tile > .content',
      label: 'dark tile !important',
      hits: contentHits,
      match: (id, theme) => theme === 'dark' && id === 'content',
      anatomy: [
        { piece: 'html.dark-theme', need: 'The page root has class dark-theme. On a light page this whole rule is absent.' },
        { piece: '.doc .openblock.cards .exampleblock.tile', need: 'The same ancestor path as the ordinary tile rule.' },
        { piece: '> .content', need: 'The element you picked has class content.' },
      ],
    },
  ];

  const INHERITED = new Set(['color', 'font-family']);
  const PROP_ORDER = ['background', 'border', 'flex', 'padding', 'display', 'color', 'font-family'];
  const RELATED: Record<string, string[]> = {
    background: [
      'background-color',
      'background-image',
      'background-repeat',
      'background-position',
      'background-size',
      'background-clip',
      'background-origin',
      'background-attachment',
    ],
    border: ['border-color', 'border-width', 'border-style', 'border-top', 'border-right', 'border-bottom', 'border-left'],
    flex: ['flex-grow', 'flex-shrink', 'flex-basis'],
    padding: ['padding-top', 'padding-right', 'padding-bottom', 'padding-left'],
  };

  let selected: NodeId = 'content';
  let theme = 'light';
  const inline = new Map<string, { value: string; important: boolean }>();
  const openSlots = new Set<string>();
  const expanded = new Set<string>();
  let litSerial: number | null = null;
  let subject = 'background';
  const serialByRule = new Map<string, number>();
  let primed = false;

  function ruleSerial(d: Decl): number {
    if (d.inline) return 0;
    const key = `${d.source}\n${d.selector}`;
    let n = serialByRule.get(key);
    if (!n) {
      n = serialByRule.size + 1;
      serialByRule.set(key, n);
    }
    return n;
  }

  function chipText(d: Decl): string {
    return d.inline ? 'inline' : `class ${ruleSerial(d)}`;
  }

  function slotKey(property: string, serial: number): string {
    return `${property}:${serial}`;
  }

  function clearSlots(property: string): void {
    for (const key of [...openSlots]) {
      if (key.startsWith(`${property}:`)) openSlots.delete(key);
    }
  }

  function showOnly(property: string, serial: number): void {
    const key = slotKey(property, serial);
    const mine = [...openSlots].filter((slot) => slot.startsWith(`${property}:`));
    const alone = !expanded.has(property) && mine.length === 1 && mine[0] === key;
    expanded.delete(property);
    clearSlots(property);
    if (!alone) openSlots.add(key);
    litSerial = serial;
    subject = property;
  }

  function prime(): void {
    if (primed) return;
    primed = true;
    for (const decl of DECLS) ruleSerial(decl);
    const brand = DECLS.find((decl) => decl.id === 'brand-bg');
    if (brand) {
      const serial = ruleSerial(brand);
      openSlots.add(slotKey('background', serial));
      litSerial = serial;
    }
  }

  function ancestors(id: NodeId): NodeId[] {
    const list: NodeId[] = [];
    let cur = PARENT[id];
    while (cur) {
      list.push(cur);
      cur = PARENT[cur];
    }
    return list;
  }

  function inlineDecl(nodeId: NodeId, property: string): Decl | null {
    const hit = inline.get(`${nodeId}:${property}`);
    if (!hit || hit.value.trim() === '') return null;
    return {
      id: `inline:${nodeId}:${property}`,
      property,
      value: hit.value,
      important: hit.important,
      specificity: [1, 0, 0],
      order: 1000,
      source: 'element.style',
      selector: 'inline style on this element',
      label: hit.important ? 'your edit !important' : 'your edit',
      hits: [nodeId],
      inline: true,
      match: () => true,
      anatomy: [
        { piece: 'style="…"', need: 'You typed this on the selected element. It is not a stylesheet rule.' },
      ],
    };
  }

  function matched(nodeId: NodeId, property: string): Decl[] {
    const found = DECLS.filter((d) => d.property === property && d.match(nodeId, theme));
    const extra = inlineDecl(nodeId, property);
    if (extra) found.push(extra);
    return found;
  }

  function layer(d: Decl): number {
    if (d.inline && d.important) return 4;
    if (d.important) return 3;
    if (d.inline) return 2;
    return 1;
  }

  function rank(a: Decl, b: Decl): number {
    if (layer(a) !== layer(b)) return layer(b) - layer(a);
    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
      if (a.specificity[i] !== b.specificity[i]) return b.specificity[i] - a.specificity[i];
    }
    return b.order - a.order;
  }

  interface Crumb {
    kind: Kind;
    decl: Decl;
    inheritedFrom: NodeId | null;
  }

  function chainFor(nodeId: NodeId, property: string): Crumb[] {
    const here = matched(nodeId, property).sort(rank);
    const crumbs: Crumb[] = [];
    if (here.length) {
      const winner = here[0];
      const losers = here.slice(1);
      for (const decl of losers.filter((d) => d.important)) {
        crumbs.push({ kind: 'important-lost', decl, inheritedFrom: null });
      }
      crumbs.push({ kind: 'active', decl: winner, inheritedFrom: null });
      for (const decl of losers.filter((d) => !d.important)) {
        crumbs.push({ kind: 'natural-lost', decl, inheritedFrom: null });
      }
      if (INHERITED.has(property)) {
        for (const anc of ancestors(nodeId)) {
          const ancMatched = matched(anc, property).sort(rank);
          if (!ancMatched.length) continue;
          crumbs.push({ kind: 'natural-lost', decl: ancMatched[0], inheritedFrom: anc });
        }
      }
      return crumbs;
    }
    if (!INHERITED.has(property)) return [];
    let foundActive = false;
    for (const anc of ancestors(nodeId)) {
      const ancMatched = matched(anc, property).sort(rank);
      if (!ancMatched.length) continue;
      crumbs.push({
        kind: foundActive ? 'natural-lost' : 'active',
        decl: ancMatched[0],
        inheritedFrom: anc,
      });
      foundActive = true;
    }
    return crumbs;
  }

  function specWords(d: Decl): string {
    if (d.inline) return d.important ? 'inline style, !important' : 'inline style';
    const [ids, classes, elements] = d.specificity;
    const bits = [`${classes} ${classes === 1 ? 'class' : 'classes'}`];
    if (elements) bits.push(`${elements} ${elements === 1 ? 'element name' : 'element names'}`);
    if (ids) bits.unshift(`${ids} id`);
    return `${bits.join(', ')} (${ids}, ${classes}, ${elements})`;
  }

  function reason(crumb: Crumb): string {
    if (crumb.kind === 'active' && crumb.inheritedFrom) {
      return `Nothing on the element you picked sets ${crumb.decl.property}. The value comes from ${NODE_LABEL[crumb.inheritedFrom]}.`;
    }
    if (crumb.kind === 'active' && crumb.decl.inline && crumb.decl.important) {
      return 'Your edit is inline and !important, so it beats stylesheet !important rules.';
    }
    if (crumb.kind === 'active' && crumb.decl.inline) {
      return 'Your edit is an inline style. It beats ordinary stylesheet rules and loses to !important.';
    }
    if (crumb.kind === 'active' && crumb.decl.important) {
      return 'This declaration is !important, and no stronger !important matches this element. Specificity does not save the rules above it in DevTools.';
    }
    if (crumb.kind === 'active') {
      return 'This is the strongest ordinary match: higher specificity, or the same specificity later in the stylesheet.';
    }
    if (crumb.kind === 'important-lost') {
      return 'This declaration is !important and still lost, because another !important is more specific or is an inline style.';
    }
    if (crumb.inheritedFrom) {
      return `Set on ${NODE_LABEL[crumb.inheritedFrom]}. Inheritance fills a property only when the element you picked does not set it.`;
    }
    if (crumb.decl.important === false) {
      return 'An ordinary declaration on this element. A matching !important, or an equal selector later in the file, beat it. A variable in the value is not why the line is inactive.';
    }
    return 'This declaration lost the cascade.';
  }

  function treeHtml(id: NodeId, hits: Set<NodeId>): string {
    const kids: NodeId[] = (Object.keys(PARENT) as NodeId[]).filter((k) => PARENT[k] === id);
    const cls = [
      selected === id ? 'is-selected' : '',
      hits.has(id) ? 'is-hit' : '',
    ].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
    const nested = kids.map((kid) => treeHtml(kid, hits)).join('');
    return `<li class="${cls}" role="treeitem" aria-selected="${selected === id}">
      <button type="button" class="elem-btn" data-node="${id}">
        <code>${NODE_LABEL[id]}</code>
      </button>
      ${nested ? `<ul role="group">${nested}</ul>` : ''}
    </li>`;
  }

  function slotOpen(property: string, serial: number): boolean {
    return expanded.has(property) || openSlots.has(slotKey(property, serial));
  }

  function render(keepProp: string | null = null): void {
    prime();
    const body = document.getElementById('inspector-body');
    if (!body) return;
    const lit = DECLS.find((decl) => ruleSerial(decl) === litSerial);
    const hits = new Set<NodeId>(lit?.hits ?? []);
    const props = PROP_ORDER.filter((p) => chainFor(selected, p).length);
    const rows = props.map((property) => rowHtml(property)).join('');
    body.innerHTML = `
      <div class="inspector-grid">
        <div class="tree-pane">
          <p class="pane-label">Elements</p>
          <ul class="elem-tree" role="tree">${treeHtml('body', hits)}</ul>
        </div>
        <div class="prop-pane">
          <p class="pane-label">Properties on ${NODE_LABEL[selected]}</p>
          <p class="status-line">Classes on this element: ${OWN_CLASSES[selected]}. Each number is one rule. A class button opens only that rule. The triangle opens every rule on the line.</p>
          ${rows || '<p>No authored properties on this element. Pick the card content or the tile.</p>'}
        </div>
      </div>`;
    if (keepProp) {
      const field = body.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(`input[data-prop="${keepProp}"]`);
      if (field) {
        const pos = field.value.length;
        field.focus();
        field.setSelectionRange(pos, pos);
      }
    }
  }

  function rowHtml(property: string): string {
    const crumbs = chainFor(selected, property);
    const active = crumbs.find((c) => c.kind === 'active');
    const typed = inline.get(`${selected}:${property}`);
    const shown = typed ? typed.value : active?.decl.value ?? '';
    const imp = typed ? typed.important : false;
    const allOpen = expanded.has(property);
    const chain = crumbs.map((c, i) => {
      const sep = i === 0 ? '' : '<span class="chain-sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span>';
      const serial = ruleSerial(c.decl);
      const pressed = slotOpen(property, serial);
      return `<li>${sep}<button type="button" class="crumb crumb-${c.kind}" data-slot="${slotKey(property, serial)}" aria-pressed="${pressed}">${chipText(c.decl)}</button></li>`;
    }).join('');
    const cards = crumbs.filter((c) => slotOpen(property, ruleSerial(c.decl))).map((c) => cardHtml(property, c)).join('');
    return `<div class="prop-row${property === subject ? ' is-subject' : ''}">
      <div class="prop-head">
        <button type="button" class="prop-name" data-subject="${property}">${property}</button>
        <input id="prop-${property}" data-prop="${property}" type="text" value="${escapeAttr(shown)}" aria-label="${property}" spellcheck="false" />
        <label class="imp-toggle"><input type="checkbox" data-imp="${property}" ${imp ? 'checked' : ''} /> !important</label>
      </div>
      <ol class="chain">${chain}<li><button type="button" class="expand-all" data-expand="${property}" aria-expanded="${allOpen}" aria-label="${allOpen ? 'Hide every class on ' + property : 'Show every class on ' + property}"></button></li></ol>
      ${cards ? `<div class="class-stack">${cards}</div>` : ''}
      ${property === subject ? relatedHtml(property) : ''}
    </div>`;
  }

  function cardHtml(property: string, crumb: Crumb): string {
    const indent = Math.max(0, crumb.decl.anatomy.length - 1);
    const winner = chainFor(selected, property).find((c) => c.kind === 'active');
    const beaten = crumb.kind !== 'active' && winner
      ? `<p class="beaten-by">Beaten by <button type="button" data-slot="${slotKey(property, ruleSerial(winner.decl))}">${chipText(winner.decl)}</button></p>`
      : '';
    const lines = crumb.decl.anatomy.map((row) =>
      `<li><code>${escapeHtml(row.piece)}</code><span>${escapeHtml(row.need)}</span></li>`,
    ).join('');
    const where = crumb.inheritedFrom ? ` · inherited from ${NODE_LABEL[crumb.inheritedFrom]}` : '';
    return `<article class="class-card is-${crumb.kind}" style="margin-left: ${indent * 0.85}rem">
      ${beaten}
      <h3>${chipText(crumb.decl)}${where}</h3>
      <p><code>${escapeHtml(crumb.decl.selector)}</code></p>
      <p>${escapeHtml(crumb.decl.value)} · ${escapeHtml(specWords(crumb.decl))} · ${escapeHtml(crumb.decl.source)}</p>
      <ol class="anatomy">${lines}</ol>
      <p class="reason">${escapeHtml(reason(crumb))}</p>
    </article>`;
  }

  function relatedHtml(property: string): string {
    const names = RELATED[property];
    if (!names?.length) return '';
    const items = names.map((name) => `<li>${escapeHtml(name)}</li>`).join('');
    return `<div class="related">
      <p>Same word in the name. Not ${escapeHtml(property)}.</p>
      <ul>${items}</ul>
    </div>`;
  }

  function escapeHtml(s: string): string {
    return s.replace(/[&<>]/g, (ch) => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;' }[ch] ?? ch));
  }

  function escapeAttr(s: string): string {
    return escapeHtml(s).replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
  }

  function eventElement(event: Event): HTMLElement | null {
    const raw = event.target;
    if (raw instanceof HTMLElement) return raw;
    if (raw instanceof Node) return raw.parentElement;
    return null;
  }

  function boot(): void {
    const root = document.querySelector('.css-styles-chain-page');
    if (!root) return;
    root.addEventListener('change', (event) => {
      const target = event.target as HTMLInputElement;
      if (target.name === 'page-theme') {
        theme = target.value;
        render();
      }
      if (target.dataset.imp) {
        const property = target.dataset.imp;
        const field = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(`input[data-prop="${property}"]`);
        inline.set(`${selected}:${property}`, {
          value: field?.value ?? '',
          important: target.checked,
        });
        render();
      }
    });
    root.addEventListener('input', (event) => {
      const target = event.target as HTMLInputElement;
      if (!target.dataset.prop) return;
      const property = target.dataset.prop;
      const imp = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(`input[data-imp="${property}"]`);
      inline.set(`${selected}:${property}`, {
        value: target.value,
        important: Boolean(imp?.checked),
      });
      expanded.delete(property);
      clearSlots(property);
      openSlots.add(slotKey(property, 0));
      litSerial = 0;
      subject = property;
      render(property);
    });
    root.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
      const target = eventElement(event);
      if (!target) return;
      const nodeBtn = target.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-node]');
      if (nodeBtn?.dataset.node) {
        selected = nodeBtn.dataset.node as NodeId;
        render();
        return;
      }
      const expandBtn = target.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-expand]');
      if (expandBtn?.dataset.expand) {
        const property = expandBtn.dataset.expand;
        if (expanded.has(property)) {
          expanded.delete(property);
          clearSlots(property);
        } else {
          clearSlots(property);
          expanded.add(property);
        }
        subject = property;
        render();
        return;
      }
      const subjectBtn = target.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-subject]');
      if (subjectBtn?.dataset.subject) {
        subject = subjectBtn.dataset.subject;
        render();
        return;
      }
      const slotBtn = target.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-slot]');
      if (slotBtn?.dataset.slot) {
        const [property, serialText] = slotBtn.dataset.slot.split(':');
        showOnly(property, Number(serialText));
        render();
      }
    });
    render();
  }

  boot();
</script>
